98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Dimension Deck is a retro top-down action roguelite built entirely in vanilla JavaScript where you fight through procedurally generated rooms using a deck of cards.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Every room you clear can hide a new card, a hidden chest, or a boss encounter. You build your deck as you explore two distinct dimensions, the Dark Ages and Old West, and the hand you've assembled determines whether you survive what's behind the next door.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (What makes it different: cards don't just execute when you press a button. Half your deck fires automatically. You're managing real-time movement and card synergies at the same time.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The closest comparison is The Binding of Isaac meets Slay the Spire, but with a twist nobody else has tried: automated trigger cards that run without any player input, turning your deck into a living system rather than a set of tools.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
