/S /H1
/P 76 0 R
/T (Game Strategy)
/E (Game Strategy)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (We decided to build a top-down roguelite with real-time card-based combat. The core idea is that the player navigates a procedurally generated map, collects cards along the way, and uses them to survive encounters without ever pausing the game.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (We chose this approach because it let us apply every topic from the course at once: object-oriented programming, data structures, relational databases, and APIs. We also wanted a real technical challenge, not just another CRUD app.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Our main references were The Binding of Isaac and Slay the Spire, but our take is different: automatic cards fire without any player input, which forces the player to think of their deck as a passive system running in parallel to their movement.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (The methodology we used was SCRUM, with 5 weekly sprints, each with concrete deliverables defined from the start. Three developers, GitHub as our shared repository.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
