/E (Modularity matters from day one. Designing the base classes \(Entity, Card, Room\) well from the start saved us weeks of refactoring later.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (SCRUM works even for small teams. Weekly sprints with defined deliverables gave us structure and kept the project moving in a clear direction.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Constant communication beats perfect communication. A short daily update prevents technical blockers and misunderstandings before they become real problems.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Early testing saves the project. Bugs we caught in Sprint 2 would have been critical if we had discovered them in Sprint 5.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 82 0 R
/E (Documenting design decisions \(the GDD\) was the best time investment we made. Whenever there was ambiguity about how something should work, the document aligned all three of us.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
