<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Implementing the active and automatic card system was the biggest technical challenge I faced. I had to think in specific triggers that the game could require at certain moments of combat.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (Enemy AI surprised me. What seems simple hides a lot of difficulties: collisions between enemies, behavior in corners, knockback. Each archetype ended up needing its own fine-tuning.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (The lack of communication on the team affected me directly in Sprint 3. I spent two days working on something that already existed. After that I made a point of sharing my progress more often, even when it was small.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (My conclusion is that coding as a team is a different skill from coding alone. It requires empathy, clarity in your code, and willingness to refactor your own work when the team needs it.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
